<SiteLayout title="Contact VYQDA | Software Development Project Enquiries" description="Contact VYQDA Technologies about custom software development, SaaS product engineering, business automation, product enquiries or application support." canonical="https://vyqda.com/contact/" active="contact">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap page-hero__inner"><p class="page-eyebrow">CONTACT VYQDA</p><h1>Tell us what you are trying to <em>make better.</em></h1><p class="page-hero__lead">A useful first conversation starts with the business challenge. Share the workflow, users, constraints and outcome you have in mind.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="button button--primary" href="mailto:contact@vyqda.com?subject=VYQDA%20project%20enquiry">Email Your Requirements <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button--secondary" href="/products/">Explore Products</a></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section" id="project-enquiry"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">START A CONVERSATION</p><h2>What would you like to solve?</h2><p>Use these prompts to prepare a clear project brief. You do not need a complete specification to begin.</p></div><div class="contact-grid"><article class="contact-method"><span class="page-card__number">01</span><h3>Custom software or application</h3><p>Describe the process, users, systems to connect and what a successful outcome would look like.</p><a href="/services/">Review development services ↗</a></article><article class="contact-method"><span class="page-card__number">02</span><h3>Existing software support</h3><p>Outline the current application, the issues you are seeing and the improvements you need.</p><a href="/about/#approach">See how we work ↗</a></article><article class="contact-method"><span class="page-card__number">03</span><h3>VYQDA software products</h3><p>Tell us the product you are considering, the team size or workflow, and any important requirements.</p><a href="/products/">Explore products ↗</a></article><article class="contact-method"><span class="page-card__number">04</span><h3>Prepare a project brief</h3><p>Include your business context, key problem, intended users, preferred timeline and known integrations.</p><p class="form-note">For an initial discussion, email contact@vyqda.com with your business context, key requirements and preferred timeline.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap page-split"><div><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">WHAT HAPPENS NEXT</p><h2>A practical discussion, not a sales script.</h2></div></div><ol class="page-list"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Understand the need</strong><p>Clarify the current workflow and the outcome you want.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Identify options</strong><p>Consider a product, integration, tailored build or phased approach.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Agree a sensible next step</strong><p>Outline the scope that needs to be understood before making commitments.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="content-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">CONTACT DETAILS</p><h2>Choose the most relevant starting point</h2><p>You can email the team with a short brief. Include only the information needed to explain the project; do not send passwords, payment card details or other sensitive credentials.</p></div><div class="contact-grid"><article class="contact-method"><span class="page-card__number">01</span><h3>Software project enquiries</h3><p>Custom applications, SaaS products, automation and integrations.</p><a href="mailto:contact@vyqda.com?subject=Software%20development%20enquiry">contact@vyqda.com ↗</a></article><article class="contact-method"><span class="page-card__number">02</span><h3>Product enquiries</h3><p>Tell us which VYQDA product you are evaluating and the workflow you need to support.</p><a href="/products/">Review products first ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>